## ✅ Fix: Cart/Wishlist Data After Logout

### Problem
When User A logs out, the cart/wishlist data remained in localStorage. When User B (unsigned) visited the site, they saw User A's old cart/wishlist data — completely wrong.

### Root Cause
The `logout` function only set `setUser(null)` and didn't clear the cart/wishlist from state or localStorage. The `load(k, d)` function in the store reads from localStorage on init, so old data persisted.

### Fix Applied to `demo-store/src/store.jsx`

**Updated `logout` function:**
```javascript
const logout = useCallback(() => {
  setUser(null);
  // Clear cart and wishlist from state + localStorage so new session starts fresh
  setCart([]);
  setWish([]);
  localStorage.removeItem("asl_cart");
  localStorage.removeItem("asl_wish");
  ping("تسجلت الخروج — نراك قريب");
}, [ping]);
```

